+- **CI red, and the re-review of round 4 (2026-11-16).** CI failed on PR #171 at 3964f80 (bridge programs, ubuntu-latest: 1 failed, 6064 passed, 66 skipped): `tests/test_tests_windowless.py::test_fix001_no_test_starts_a_program_around_the_default` read the acceptance case `husky-before-python-c` (line 397 of the supervisor's acceptance file, since round 3's brief) as a launch around the windowless default, its string literal holding `os.system(`. The literal was split into two concatenated parts, the string unchanged; no guard code changed and no builder ran. The new head was read again under the class line `behaviour - CI red ... the windowless scan`: Review A and Review B approved, both confirming the line at 3964f80; `verify TASK-063-r4` OK, `premerge TASK-063-r4 171` OK; CI green on both platforms at b76e187, merged as b05fbc8. Lesson: the supervisor's acceptance file runs the increment's own tests locally but not the suite-wide scans over `tests/`; an acceptance case that writes interpreter code as a string meets the windowless scan, so such a string is written in parts from the start.
